# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build, separate from
# the Dockerfile's own .dockerignore (which governs the Docker build context
# once uploaded). Without this file, gcloud silently falls back to excluding
# whatever .gitignore excludes — which broke /health's git SHA: build-info.json
# is gitignored (regenerated every build, never checked in), so before this
# file existed, gcloud dropped it from the upload before the Docker build
# ever ran, and the deployed /health always read back "unknown" no matter
# what scripts/write-build-info.mjs wrote. This file's job is exactly to NOT
# inherit that exclusion.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.output
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
